  "notes": "R52c targets lifecycle event notification coverage in hybrid mode. PRIMARY evidence (E2, E3, E4, E6, E7, E11) establishes core notification requirements across five categories: lifecycle event triggers, email delivery with retry, reminder scheduling, administrative notifications, content templates, user preferences, and logging. E8 introduces a cross-cutting concern about promotional content in reminder emails that creates a gap in preference handling rules. E5, E9, E10 provide implementation context confirming lifecycle event triggers and notification generation rules. CONTEXT evidence (E13-E20) establishes neighboring rent lifecycle and delivery lifecycle requirements but does not override target-specific rules. Key operative rules are drawn directly from E2 (TOOLCHAIN-CONF-NOTIFICATION-01) and E11 (detailed specification sections 5.1-5.7). Exceptions and gaps reflect unresolved policy decisions in E7 (approval-related non-optional messages) and E8 (promotional messaging consent model). Conflicts center on E3 comment regarding retry threshold configurability.\" Filtered abstract or low-relevance operative statements: System shall send notifications via email to the user account email address | System shall ensure notification delivery is reliable with retry support on failure | System shall allow configuration of reminder timing without code changes",
